+# SmartTube Mobile fork
+
+This fork adds an Android phone build flavor while retaining SmartTube's existing
+service, OAuth, playback, SponsorBlock, settings, and update architecture.
+
+## Build
+
+The initial development APK is built with:
+
+```sh
+./gradlew :smarttubetv:assembleStmobileDebug
+```
+
+The package id is `app.smarttube.mobile`, so it can be installed alongside the
+official SmartTube TV application. The APK output is named using the upstream
+variant naming logic and is written under `smarttubetv/build/outputs/apk/`.
+
+## Current mobile surface
+
+- portrait-first feed with one full-width video card per row
+- two-column feed in landscape
+- horizontally scrollable touch section navigation
+- native search field and five-item bottom navigation
+- back button and Android Back support
+- synced subscriptions and history when a YouTube account is activated
+- signed-out Home fallback with the original local channels
+- account connection and switching in a touch-friendly Settings page
+- correctly scaled 16:9 thumbnails, improved typography, and duration badges
+- manual in-app GitHub release update check (signed releases required to install over an existing build)
+- tap to play and long-press for the existing video menu
+- existing SmartTube playback, SponsorBlock, and advanced settings architecture
+
+## Account sync
+
+Settings → YouTube sync → Connect opens YouTube's device activation flow at
+https://yt.be/activate. The app uses SmartTube's existing account/token storage
+and content service; it does not need a separate Google Cloud OAuth client,
+and does not save your credentials in this mobile patch repository.
+
+After account activation, Home and Subscriptions use the account's live YouTube
+subscriptions. History uses SmartTube's logged-in history service and may be
+unavailable if YouTube history is disabled. Signing out returns Home to the
+original local-channel fallback.
+
+## Updates and Android signing
+
+Settings → Check for updates looks for the latest GitHub release tagged v8,
+v9, and so forth, and offers the ARM64 APK download. Replacing an installed
+Android application requires the **same signing key** for every release.
+An APK built with a new debug key cannot update the older v6 debug APK in
+place; a one-time uninstall may be required. Production releases must use
+a securely stored, persistent signing key.
+
+The TV build flavors are intentionally unchanged.
